1:# DEVDESK-341 — Footer: replace the braille spinner by the shared activity dot
8:## 0. Blocking question (to the user)
26:## 1. Inventory (verified in code, commit 56166bf8)
28:### 1.1 The 8 router frame consumers (`m.footer.SetSpinnerFrame(msg.RenderedFrame)`)
43:### 1.2 Out of scope (Q1): view-owned `spinner.Model` feeding a `Spinner: true` status
58:## 2. Q5: do the view-owned spinners respect `app.motion: static` and the blur?
71:## 3. Non-functional requirements
89:## 4. Options
104:## 5. Interfaces (step 1)
149:## 6. Implementation plan
155:### Step 1: `FooterMessage` learns the activity dot (S)
180:### Step 2: migrate the 8 router consumers (S each, **parallelizable 2a–2h after step 1**)
211:### Step 3: guards (S–M, after all of step 2)
257:### Step 4: documentation pass (S, after step 3; can run in parallel with step 5)
272:### Step 5: retire the braille frame from the router (S–M, optional, separable)
312:### Step 6: final check (XS)
319:### Step 7: only if §0 is answered B: explorer loads on the shared dot (S)
331:## 7. Order and parallelism
339:## 8. Risks and irreversible points
349:## 9. Effort (re-estimate)
diff --git i/internal/ui/components/footer_message.go w/internal/ui/components/footer_message.go
